---
import SealedSection from '../seal/SealedSection.astro';
import ShotCarousel from '../ui/ShotCarousel.tsx';

import trustPipeline from '../../assets/concepts/trust-pipeline.svg?raw';
import chunked from '../../assets/concepts/chunked-classification.svg?raw';
import classifierPhases from '../../assets/concepts/classifier-phases.svg?raw';
import agentTurnShot from '../../assets/shots/agent-turn.svg';
import classifierShot from '../../assets/shots/classifier.svg';

const sealText =
  'Trust pipeline: every untrusted tool result is sanitized, classified, then decided. Shaped results take a sanitize-only lane with no classifier round trip. The default install classifies in-process with two embedded BERT gates, and the extraction sentinel is opt-in.';
---

<SealedSection label="trust" sealText={sealText} id="trust">
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="prose-measure">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-vx-ink">Trust pipeline.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Every untrusted result goes through <strong>sanitize, classify, decide</strong>, fail closed.{' '}
        <code class="mono">Bash</code>, <code class="mono">WebFetch</code>, <code class="mono">WebSearch</code>, <code class="mono">Read</code>,{' '}
        supervised process output, and third-party repository text all classify, unconditionally. Shaped results whose shape the
        harness knows, like <code class="mono">Grep</code>, <code class="mono">Glob</code>, <code class="mono">Write</code>, and{' '}
        <code class="mono">Edit</code>, take a sanitize-only lane and skip the round trip.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Long documents are classified in bounded chunks with overlap. The verdict is the strictest
        across all chunks, not the first and not the average.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={trustPipeline} /></div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={chunked} /></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
    <div class="order-2 lg:order-1 rounded-lg border border-vx-ink p-2" aria-hidden="true">
      <Fragment set:html={classifierPhases} />
    </div>
    <div class="prose-measure order-1 lg:order-2">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-vx-ink">The classifier ships in the binary.</h3>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The default download embeds its own guardrails. Two small BERT sequence classifiers run{' '}
        <strong>in-process</strong> — pure Go, no cgo, no Python, no API key — so a fresh install
        classifies untrusted content before you have configured a provider at all.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        <strong>Phase 1</strong> is prompt saturation, <strong>phase 2</strong> is jailbreak, and they
        run concurrently over the same token windows. If either fires, the content already fails
        closed and the fold returns immediately. <strong>Phase 3</strong> is a narrowed LLM sentinel
        covering only <code class="mono">DATA_EXTRACTION</code> and <code class="mono">MODEL_EXTRACTION</code>,{' '}
        the two categories no purpose-built model reaches — and it broadens to cover{' '}
        <code class="mono">JAILBREAK</code> when phase 2 is <em>deferred to phase 3</em> on a binary
        without an embedded jailbreak model.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        Phase 3 is opt-in, and the switch is a setting you already have: it runs only when{' '}
        <code class="mono">classifier.provider</code> <em>and</em> <code class="mono">classifier.model</code> are
        both set. The classifier model picker is restricted to classifier-appropriate choices — the
        five curated HuggingFace BERT models, or the TypeSafe Jev Decisions model{' '}
        (<code class="mono">typesafe/jev-1.13</code>) tool-call gate on OpenRouter — with a broad-model
        warning on custom, llama-server and Ollama providers. Leave the fields clear and the classify
        path makes no network call at all — and says so on the <code class="mono">/model</code> phase-3
        row rather than implying coverage it does not have.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-vx-ink/80">
        The local models hard-error past 512 tokens instead of truncating, so the ML path windows by
        BERT tokens with overlap and fails closed past its window ceiling. A binary whose embedded
        model fails to load is a startup error, never a quiet downgrade. Verdicts are cached by the
        hash of the sanitized content <em>plus the classifier identity</em>, so switching stacks never
        serves a verdict another one produced.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 max-w-[72ch]">
    <ShotCarousel
      client:load
      shots={[
        { src: classifierShot.src, alt: 'The /model classifier rows showing kind, phase 1, phase 2 and phase 3', caption: '/model, classifier kind and phase rows' },
        { src: agentTurnShot.src, alt: 'A streaming agent turn with a collapsed Bash preview', caption: 'streaming turn, collapsed Bash preview' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>
</SealedSection>
